<title>SWEDEN: Sweden's Frontline approves ship purchase.</title>
<headline>Sweden's Frontline approves ship purchase.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>An extraordinary meeting of shareholders in shipping company Frontline AB approved a proposal to acquire six tankers, five VLCC's and one Suezmax together with two OBO vessels.</p>
<p>The vessels will be bought by the issue of 55.3 million new shares in Frontline, raising its share capital by 1.1 billion crowns to 2.0 billion.</p>
<p>After the purchase Frontline will control a wholly owned fleet of 3.1 million dwt.</p>
<p>-- Tony Austin, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
</text>
